Filed by langertha-llm-advisor, 2026-09-01. Docs read 2026-09-01 at platform.claude.com
(docs.claude.com / docs.anthropic.com now redirect there). No live calls. Three separate wire
facts that each make a Langertha AnthropicBase request wrong or a Response empty. Grouped because
they are all "the Anthropic wire moved under a field we already emit or read".

## 1. temperature is deprecated and 400s with a non-default value on current Opus models

`Role::AnthropicCompatible::chat_request` (:183-185) and `chat_stream_request` (:408-410) emit

    $self->has_temperature ? ( temperature => $self->temperature ) : ()

unconditionally whenever the attribute is set. `Role::Temperature` is composed by
`Engine::AnthropicBase`, so it is set-able on every Anthropic-family engine.

Anthropic changelog 2026-05-28, verbatim: "Setting the sampling parameters `temperature`, `top_p`,
or `top_k` to a non-default value returns a 400 error on Claude Opus 4.8, same as on Claude Opus
4.7." The Messages API reference now lists `temperature` / `top_p` / `top_k` as **deprecated**.

So `Langertha::Engine::Anthropic->new(model => 'claude-opus-4-8', temperature => 0.5)` is a hard
400. The set of affected models is growing, not shrinking. Options: model-gated suppression (the
`Engine::OpenAI::_max_tokens_key` precedent), an `around engine_capabilities` clearing
`temperature` for those models, or at minimum a POD warning. Note it cannot be fixed purely in
`engine_capabilities` today because the flag is engine-wide, not model-wide -- same root cause as
k133 point 2.

Source: https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/release-notes/api ,
https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/messages

## 2. thinking.display now defaults to "omitted" -- $response->thinking is empty on every current model

https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking (read 2026-09-01).
`thinking: {type:"adaptive"}` takes an optional `display`: `"summarized"` | `"omitted"` |
`"updates"` (the last is beta, header `thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18`).

The default is **"omitted"** on Fable 5.1, Mythos 5.1, Fable 5, Mythos 5, Opus 5, Sonnet 5,
Opus 4.8, Opus 4.7 and Mythos Preview. It is `"summarized"` only on Opus 4.6, Sonnet 4.6 and
earlier. Under `display: "omitted"` **no `thinking_delta` events are emitted at all** -- the
thinking block opens, emits one `signature_delta`, and closes.

`Langertha::Reasoning::to_anthropic` emits `thinking => { type => 'adaptive' }` with no `display`
key, so on every model in that first list `$response->thinking` comes back empty --
`Role::AnthropicCompatible::chat_response:303` collects `thinking` blocks whose `thinking` field
is the empty string. Not a crash, just a silently blank feature on the default path.

Fix direction: let the caller ask for summaries. Either a `thinking_display` knob on
`Role::ReasoningEffort` serialized by `Langertha::Reasoning::to_anthropic`, or make
`display => 'summarized'` the Langertha default (a product call -- summaries cost tokens). At
minimum POD the fact, because "Anthropic returns no thinking" reads as a Langertha bug otherwise.
Relates to k129 (streamed thinking deltas): a stream test asserting non-empty thinking on a
current Claude model will fail for this reason, not for a parser reason.

Also from the same family, and NOT read by Langertha today:
`usage.output_tokens_details.thinking_tokens` (shipped 2026-05-27; on the streaming path it
appears only on the final `message_delta`). That is the only way to see that thinking happened
when `display` is `"omitted"`.

## 3. Anthropic prompt caching: two facts worth POD'ing

Both from https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching (read 2026-09-01).

(a) The top-level `cache_control` form Langertha emits (`Langertha::PromptCache::to_anthropic`)
    is CORRECT and documented -- it is the "Automatic caching" feature shipped 2026-02-19:
    "Instead of placing `cache_control` on individual content blocks, add a single `cache_control`
    field at the top level of your request body. The system automatically applies the cache
    breakpoint to the last cacheable block." It composes with block-level breakpoints and consumes
    one of the 4 available slots. No change needed -- recording it so nobody "fixes" it later.

(b) Silent no-op trap: the minimum cacheable prefix is model-dependent -- 512 tokens
    (Fable 5.1 / Mythos 5.1 / Opus 5 / Fable 5 / Mythos 5), 1,024 (Opus 4.8, Sonnet 5, Sonnet 4.6,
    Sonnet 4.5), 2,048 (Opus 4.7, Mythos Preview), 4,096 (Opus 4.6, Opus 4.5, Haiku 4.5).
    Verbatim: "Shorter prompts cannot be cached, even if marked with `cache_control`. No error is
    returned; the request is processed without caching." So `prompt_cache => 1` succeeding proves
    nothing; only `usage.cache_read_input_tokens` / `cache_creation_input_tokens` does.
    t/86_live_prompt_cache.t already asserts on usage rather than on a 200 -- correct, keep it.
